    "narrative": "As we navigate the final stretch of the 2026 campaign, **Lawrence Butler** stands out as our premier option today. With a 74.61 efficiency score, he benefits from a favorable matchup against Wesneski and a projected move to the #2 hole, which maximizes his exposure to prime run-producing scenarios. Alongside him, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (68.84) remains a mandatory start despite a lukewarm BvP history; his floor is bolstered by the high volume of opportunities at the #2 spot. **Will Smith** is our high-upside leverage play in the utility slot; while facing a lefty, the 4.63 xERA of Wilkinson combined with favorable wind conditions provides a distinct edge, pushing his score to a robust 63.61.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved balancing the scarcity of speed against raw power. While **Justin Crawford** offers the elite sprint speed we covet for the SB category, his placement in the #9 hole drags his efficiency down to a marginal 49.29, keeping him in the lineup only due to the lack of a higher-projected alternative among the reserves. We are monitoring **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Zack Gelof**, and **Lawrence Butler** closely, as their final lineup confirmation is pending. Should these hitters shift significantly down their respective orders, we may need to pivot. **Gavin Sheets** and **JJ Bleday** represent our lowest-ceiling starts today at 51.70 and 51.27, respectively; they are barely outperforming the bench threshold, but with **Tyler Freeman**, **Matt Chapman**, **Daulton Varsho**, and **Luis Arraez** currently unavailable, we lack the depth to improve our standing in the aggregate without sacrificing critical positional utility. \n\nWe continue to track the developmental progress of **Dylan Beavers**, **Masyn Winn**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Alex Freeland**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Braden Montgomery**, but for today\u2019s 5x5 Roto push, the aforementioned starters must carry the load. Pay special attention to the **Bryce Harper** matchup against Jax; his 60.82 score is supported by strong peripheral metrics, though he faces the toughest opposing arm of the day (3.61 xERA). We are locked in for the late-season push\u2014maintain discipline on game caps as we monitor these margins.",
